<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP year steel despatches up 4 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP year steel despatches up 4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Tuesday steel despatches rose four percent in the year to May 31, 1997, but raw steelmake fell two percent over the same period.  </p>
<p>BHP said the fall in raw steel production was mainly a result of Newcastle production being restricted by a 72-day shutdown for the reline of number four blastfurnace.</p>
<p>It said May raw steel production was affected by a 24 hour industrial stoppage at Australian steelworks and maintenance at Newcastle. Last month, BHP, Australia's largest steelmaker, said it would shut down its Newcastle plant by 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;Despatches were higher for both May and the year to May with export despatches from international operations other than New Zealand steel growing by 32 percent for the 12 months to May,&quot; BHP said.  </p>
